1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"phase-1--1b-effort-tracking","kind":"phase-article","route":"/roadmap/phase-1/1b-effort-tracking","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/phase-1/1b-effort-tracking","sourceHash":"1e133cd2f1d17b566effe66ee08537ad6456387b98c9d0f976d0c182546306ed","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T23:11:38.917Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"1B — Effort Tracking","zh":"1B — 记录投入"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"what-youre-doing","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"What You're Doing","zh":"你要做什么"}},{"id":"segment-0002","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Now that you have your feet under you, it's time to add something that will dramatically increase your chances of success: tracking your effort. In our experience working with hundreds of language learners, effort tracking is directly correlated with better outcomes.","zh":"现在你已经初步适应，是时候加入一项能显著提高成功概率的做法：记录自己的投入。根据我们与数百名语言学习者合作的经验，记录投入与更好的学习结果直接相关。"}},{"id":"segment-0003","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Learning a language is a long process, and day-to-day progress is nearly invisible. It's like growing taller as a kid — you never noticed it happening, but it was. Without something concrete to look at, it won't <em>feel</em> like you're making progress, and that can be demoralizing. Tracking gives you that concrete evidence.","zh":"学习一门语言是个漫长的过程，而每天的进步几乎难以察觉。这就像小时候长高一样——你从未注意到它发生，但它确实发生了。如果没有具体的东西可以观察，你就不会<em>感觉</em>自己在进步，这可能会令人泄气。记录能为你提供这种具体的证据。"}},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"It also lets you make informed improvements. If something isn't working, you can look at what you've actually been doing (not what you <em>think</em> you've been doing — humans have bad memories) and adjust. And if you ever ask for help from the community, having a real log of your learning is invaluable.","zh":"记录也能帮助你做出有依据的改进。如果某件事不起作用，你可以查看自己实际做了什么（而不是<em>以为</em>自己做了什么——人的记忆并不可靠），然后进行调整。如果你需要向社区求助，一份真实的学习记录也会非常有价值。"}},{"id":"whats-new","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"What's New","zh":"有什么新内容"}},{"id":"segment-0006","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Your language learning activities stay the same as 1A — you're still doing vocab study, grammar/sound priming, and the Noticing Game. The only new piece is the tracking itself.","zh":"你的语言学习活动与 1A 相同——你仍然会学习词汇，进行语法和发音预热，以及玩注意力游戏。唯一新增的部分就是记录本身。"}},{"id":"segment-0007","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Effort and Time Tracking</strong> — You'll start logging what you do each day and how long you spend on it. The goal isn't perfect accuracy; it's building awareness of your routine. A stopwatch and a simple log is all you need, though purpose-built tools make it much easier. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/effort-and-time-tracking\">Effort and Time Tracking</a>","zh":"<strong>投入与时间记录</strong>——你将开始记录每天做了什么，以及在每项活动上花了多长时间。目标不是做到绝对精确，而是建立对自己学习安排的觉察。你只需要一块秒表和一份简单记录，当然，专门设计的工具会让这件事容易得多。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/effort-and-time-tracking\">投入与时间记录</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0008","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>The Refold App</strong> — We built an app specifically for language learners to make tracking easy. It lets you set habits, log daily actions, and see breakdowns of how you're spending your time. It also has built-in recommendations for each phase. You don't have to use it — any tracking method works for this phase — but we designed a tool specifically for this purpose. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-refold-app\">The Refold App</a>","zh":"<strong>Refold 应用</strong>——我们专门为语言学习者开发了一款应用，让记录变得简单。你可以设置习惯、记录每日行动，并查看时间分配明细。它还为每个阶段提供内置建议。你不必使用它——本阶段任何记录方法都可以——但我们确实为这个目的专门设计了一款工具。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-refold-app\">Refold 应用</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0009","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Habit Health</strong> — This is a concept (and a metric in the Refold App) that measures how consistently you're hitting your daily learning goals. An 80%+ Habit Health over 14 days means you're building a sustainable routine, which is the real goal of this sub-phase.","zh":"<strong>习惯健康度</strong>——这是一个概念，也是 Refold 应用中的一项指标，用于衡量你坚持完成每日学习目标的稳定程度。连续 14 天保持 80% 以上的习惯健康度，意味着你正在建立可持续的学习安排，而这正是本子阶段的真正目标。"}},{"id":"segment-0010","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"This is instead of focusing on <strong>streaks</strong>, which are the most common metric used in language learning apps. They're <em>okay</em>, but we find that Habit Health is much more indicative of a healthy language routine. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/habit-health\">Habit Health</a>","zh":"这意味着不要把重点放在<strong>连续打卡</strong>上，这是语言学习应用最常用的指标。它们<em>还可以</em>，但我们发现，习惯健康度更能反映健康的语言学习安排。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/habit-health\">习惯健康度</a>"}},{"id":"your-routine","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Your Routine","zh":"你的学习安排"}},{"id":"segment-0012","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Same split as 1A:","zh":"与 1A 的比例相同："}},{"id":"segment-0013","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"<strong>Priming:</strong> 50%","zh":"<strong>预热：</strong>50%"},{"en":"<strong>Interactive Immersion:</strong> 50%","zh":"<strong>互动沉浸：</strong>50%"}]},{"id":"segment-0014","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The only difference is that now you're tracking how much time you spend on each, so you know the actual ratio instead of guessing. In the Refold App, you can check the \"Reports\" tab to see graphs of how you're spending your time.","zh":"唯一的区别是，现在你会记录在每项活动上花了多少时间，因此你知道实际比例，而不是靠猜。在 Refold 应用中，你可以查看“报告”标签，了解自己的时间分配图表。"}},{"id":"segment-0015","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Just remember that it doesn't need to be <em>exactly</em> 50/50. No one is a robot. But if you're doing something closer to 60/40, you know you should adjust slightly.","zh":"记住，不需要<em>恰好</em>达到 50/50。没有人是机器人。但如果你的比例更接近 60/40，就说明你应该稍微调整一下。"}},{"id":"sample-daily-schedule","type":"heading","level":3,"content":{"en":"Sample Daily Schedule","zh":"每日安排示例"}},{"id":"segment-0017","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Vocab study: 15-20 mins","zh":"词汇学习：15–20 分钟"},{"en":"Grammar study: 5-10 mins","zh":"语法学习：5–10 分钟"},{"en":"Sound study: 5-10 mins","zh":"发音学习：5–10 分钟"},{"en":"The Noticing Game (with comprehensible input): 30+ mins","zh":"注意力游戏（结合可理解输入）：30 分钟以上"},{"en":"<em>Plus: logging all of the above</em>","zh":"<em>另外：记录以上所有活动</em>"}]},{"id":"when-to-move-on","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"When to Move On","zh":"何时进入下一阶段"}},{"id":"segment-0019","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Move to 1C when you:","zh":"满足以下条件后进入 1C："}},{"id":"segment-0020","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Are consistently tracking the time you spend with the language","zh":"持续记录自己花在这门语言上的时间"},{"en":"Have 80%+ Habit Health for the last 14 days <a href=\"/roadmap/library/habit-health\">Habit Health</a>","zh":"过去 14 天的习惯健康度达到 80% 以上 <a href=\"/roadmap/library/habit-health\">习惯健康度</a>"}]},{"id":"research-and-reasoning","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Research and Reasoning","zh":"研究与依据"}},{"id":"segment-0022","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Effort tracking works because it engages metacognition — your ability to monitor and reflect on your own learning. Research on self-regulated learning (Zimmerman, 2002) demonstrates that learners who actively track their progress and adjust their strategies outperform those who don't. In language learning specifically, maintaining awareness of what you're actually doing (versus what you think you're doing) lets you identify patterns, spot problems early, and make evidence-based adjustments rather than relying on faulty intuition.","zh":"努力追踪之所以有效，是因为它调动了元认知——也就是监控和反思自身学习的能力。关于自我调节学习的研究（Zimmerman，2002）表明，主动追踪进度并调整策略的学习者，表现优于不这样做的学习者。具体到语言学习中，清楚意识到自己实际上在做什么（而不是以为自己在做什么），能帮助你发现规律、及早识别问题，并依据证据进行调整，而不是依赖不可靠的直觉。"}},{"id":"segment-0023","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The neurological basis for why consistency (either through streaks or habit health) matters comes from skill acquisition theory: repeated practice moves language abilities from conscious, controlled processing to automatic, intuitive processing (DeKeyser, 2007).","zh":"一致性（无论通过连续学习记录还是习惯健康度来维持）之所以重要，其神经学基础来自技能习得理论：重复练习会让语言能力从有意识、受控制的加工，转变为自动、直觉式的加工（DeKeyser，2007）。"}},{"id":"segment-0024","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The key word is <em>repeated</em> — sporadic effort produces sporadic results. Tracking habits helps ensure the repetition is actually happening. The 80% Habit Health target balances consistency with the reality that perfect attendance is neither necessary nor realistic; research suggests that moderate, regular practice beats ambitious but inconsistent schedules (Kim &amp; Webb, 2022).","zh":"关键词是<em>重复</em>——零散的努力只能带来零散的结果。追踪习惯有助于确保重复练习确实发生。80%的习惯健康度目标，在一致性与现实情况之间取得了平衡：每天完美出勤既无必要，也不现实；研究表明，适度而规律的练习胜过雄心勃勃却缺乏一致性的计划（Kim &amp; Webb，2022）。"}}],"cards":[]},"siteBasePath":"/my_learning_docs"}]
